ins</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The contributions of replication orientation, gene direction, and signal sequences to base-composition asymmetries in bacterial genomes</article-title><source>J Mol Evol</source><year>2000</year><volume>50</volume><fpage>249</fpage><lpage>257</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10754068</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Rocha</surname><given-names>EPC</given-names></name><name><surname>Danchin</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Viari</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Universal replication biases in bacteria</article-title><source>Mol Microbiol</source><year>1999</year><volume>32</volume><fpage>11</fpage><lpage>16</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10216855</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1046/j.1365-2958.1999.01334.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>McInerney</surname><given-names>JO</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Replicational and transcriptional selection on codon usage in <italic>Borrelia burgdorferi </italic></article-title><source>PNAS</source><year>1998</year><volume>95</volume><fpage>10698</fpage><lpage>10703</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9724767</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1073/pnas.95.18.10698</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B25"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lafay</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Lloyd</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>McLean</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Devine</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Sharp</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolfe</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></pers